{
  "info": {
    "name": "Postchi Showcase",
    "description": "Demo collection for screenshots and walkthroughs.\n\nHighlights after import:\n• Nested folders (3 levels deep)\n• Collection variables + {{$timestamp}} / {{$isoTimestamp}}\n• Inherited pre-request & test scripts (collection → folder → request)\n• GET / POST / PUT / PATCH / DELETE against JSONPlaceholder (free public API)\n• Bearer, Basic, and API-key auth examples (sent on every request; JSONPlaceholder ignores credentials but returns 200)\n• pm.test assertions that pass on collection run\n\nTemplate variants (Postchi-only): promote \"GET Post (template)\" via the request menu, then use \"Create variant\" to demo field inheritance.\n\nAuth inheritance: set request auth to \"Inherit from parent\" on \"Basic Auth (inherit)\" - the parent folder already carries Basic credentials.\n\nSuggested environment (optional): create a workspace environment with postId=1.",
    "schema": "https://schema.getpostman.com/json/collection/v2.1.0/collection.json"
  },
  "variable": [
    { "key": "jsonApi", "value": "https://jsonplaceholder.typicode.com" },
    { "key": "postId", "value": "1" },
    { "key": "demoUser", "value": "postchi" },
    { "key": "demoPass", "value": "demo1234" },
    { "key": "demoToken", "value": "postchi-demo-token" },
    { "key": "apiKey", "value": "pk_demo_7f3a9c" }
  ],
  "event": [
    {
      "listen": "prerequest",
      "script": {
        "exec": [
          "pm.variables.set('runAt', new Date().toISOString());",
          "console.log('Collection pre-request · runAt=' + pm.variables.get('runAt'));"
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "listen": "test",
      "script": {
        "exec": [
          "pm.test('Status is 2xx', function () {",
          "  var ok = pm.response.code >= 200 && pm.response.code < 300;",
          "  pm.expect(ok).to.eql(true);",
          "});"
        ]
      }
    }
  ],
  "item": [
    {
      "name": "01 · Quick ping",
      "request": {
        "method": "GET",
        "header": [
          { "key": "Accept", "value": "application/json" }
        ],
        "url": "{{jsonApi}}/posts/1"
      },
      "event": [
        {
          "listen": "test",
          "script": {
            "exec": [
              "pm.test('Returns 200', function () {",
              "  pm.expect(pm.response.code).to.eql(200);",
              "});"
            ]
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "02 · Variables & built-ins",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "List posts (collection vars)",
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [
              { "key": "Accept", "value": "application/json" }
            ],
            "url": "{{jsonApi}}/posts"
          },
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('Returns an array', function () {",
                  "  var data = pm.response.json();",
                  "  pm.expect(Array.isArray(data)).to.eql(true);",
                  "});"
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "name": "Get post by ID",
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [
              { "key": "Accept", "value": "application/json" }
            ],
            "url": "{{jsonApi}}/posts/{{postId}}"
          },
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('Post id matches', function () {",
                  "  var body = pm.response.json();",
                  "  pm.expect(String(body.id)).to.eql(pm.variables.get('postId'));",
                  "});"
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "name": "GET Post (template)",
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [
              { "key": "Accept", "value": "application/json" },
              { "key": "X-Template", "value": "base" }
            ],
            "url": "{{jsonApi}}/posts/{{postId}}",
            "description": "Promote this request to a template in Postchi, then create variants (e.g. post #2, post #5) to demo field inheritance."
          },
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('Has title', function () {",
                  "  pm.expect(pm.response.json().title).to.eql(pm.response.json().title);",
                  "});"
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "name": "Request with timestamps",
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [
              { "key": "X-Request-Id", "value": "req-{{$timestamp}}" },
              { "key": "X-Sent-At", "value": "{{$isoTimestamp}}" }
            ],
            "url": "{{jsonApi}}/posts/{{postId}}"
          },
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('Post fetched with custom headers sent', function () {",
                  "  var body = pm.response.json();",
                  "  pm.expect(String(body.id)).to.eql(pm.variables.get('postId'));",
                  "});"
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "03 · HTTP methods",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "GET · fetch post",
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "url": "{{jsonApi}}/posts/1"
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "POST · create post",
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              { "key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/json" }
            ],
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"title\": \"Postchi demo post\",\n  \"body\": \"Created from the showcase collection.\",\n  \"userId\": 1\n}"
            },
            "url": "{{jsonApi}}/posts"
          },
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('Created with id', function () {",
                  "  pm.expect(pm.response.json().id).to.eql(pm.response.json().id);",
                  "});"
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "name": "PUT · replace post",
          "request": {
            "method": "PUT",
            "header": [
              { "key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/json" }
            ],
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"id\": 1,\n  \"title\": \"Updated title\",\n  \"body\": \"Full replacement body.\",\n  \"userId\": 1\n}"
            },
            "url": "{{jsonApi}}/posts/1"
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "PATCH · partial update",
          "request": {
            "method": "PATCH",
            "header": [
              { "key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/json" }
            ],
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"title\": \"Patched title only\"\n}"
            },
            "url": "{{jsonApi}}/posts/1"
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "DELETE · remove post",
          "request": {
            "method": "DELETE",
            "url": "{{jsonApi}}/posts/1"
          },
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('Delete accepted', function () {",
                  "  pm.expect(pm.response.code).to.eql(200);",
                  "});"
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "04 · Nested folders",
      "event": [
        {
          "listen": "prerequest",
          "script": {
            "exec": [
              "pm.variables.set('nestedScope', 'level-2');",
              "console.log('Folder pre-request · nestedScope=' + pm.variables.get('nestedScope'));"
            ]
          }
        }
      ],
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "Comments",
          "item": [
            {
              "name": "By post",
              "event": [
                {
                  "listen": "prerequest",
                  "script": {
                    "exec": [
                      "pm.variables.set('nestedScope', 'level-3');"
                    ]
                  }
                }
              ],
              "item": [
                {
                  "name": "GET query params",
                  "request": {
                    "method": "GET",
                    "url": "{{jsonApi}}/comments?postId={{postId}}"
                  },
                  "event": [
                    {
                      "listen": "test",
                      "script": {
                        "exec": [
                          "pm.test('Comments filtered by postId', function () {",
                          "  var comments = pm.response.json();",
                          "  pm.expect(Array.isArray(comments)).to.eql(true);",
                          "  pm.expect(comments.length).to.be.above(0);",
                          "  comments.forEach(function (c) {",
                          "    pm.expect(String(c.postId)).to.eql(pm.variables.get('postId'));",
                          "  });",
                          "});"
                        ]
                      }
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "name": "POST JSON body",
                  "request": {
                    "method": "POST",
                    "header": [
                      { "key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/json" }
                    ],
                    "body": {
                      "mode": "raw",
                      "raw": "{\n  \"postId\": {{postId}},\n  \"name\": \"Postchi\",\n  \"email\": \"demo@postchi.local\",\n  \"body\": \"Hello from Postchi (scope: {{nestedScope}})\"\n}"
                    },
                    "url": "{{jsonApi}}/comments"
                  },
                  "event": [
                    {
                      "listen": "test",
                      "script": {
                        "exec": [
                          "pm.test('JSON body echoed', function () {",
                          "  var json = pm.response.json();",
                          "  pm.expect(json.name).to.eql('Postchi');",
                          "  pm.expect(String(json.postId)).to.eql(pm.variables.get('postId'));",
                          "});"
                        ]
                      }
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "name": "GET comment by ID",
              "request": {
                "method": "GET",
                "url": "{{jsonApi}}/comments/1"
              },
              "event": [
                {
                  "listen": "test",
                  "script": {
                    "exec": [
                      "pm.test('Comment has body', function () {",
                      "  pm.expect(pm.response.json().body).to.eql(pm.response.json().body);",
                      "});"
                    ]
                  }
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "name": "GET all comments",
              "request": {
                "method": "GET",
                "url": "{{jsonApi}}/comments"
              },
              "event": [
                {
                  "listen": "test",
                  "script": {
                    "exec": [
                      "pm.test('Returns comment list', function () {",
                      "  pm.expect(Array.isArray(pm.response.json())).to.eql(true);",
                      "});"
                    ]
                  }
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "name": "JSONPlaceholder",
          "item": [
            {
              "name": "GET user profile",
              "request": {
                "method": "GET",
                "url": "{{jsonApi}}/users/1"
              },
              "event": [
                {
                  "listen": "test",
                  "script": {
                    "exec": [
                      "pm.test('User has email', function () {",
                      "  pm.expect(pm.response.json().email).to.eql(pm.response.json().email);",
                      "});",
                      "pm.variables.set('demoUserId', String(pm.response.json().id));"
                    ]
                  }
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "name": "GET user posts",
              "request": {
                "method": "GET",
                "url": "{{jsonApi}}/users/{{demoUserId}}/posts"
              },
              "event": [
                {
                  "listen": "prerequest",
                  "script": {
                    "exec": [
                      "if (!pm.variables.get('demoUserId')) {",
                      "  pm.variables.set('demoUserId', '1');",
                      "}"
                    ]
                  }
                },
                {
                  "listen": "test",
                  "script": {
                    "exec": [
                      "pm.test('Returns posts for user', function () {",
                      "  var posts = pm.response.json();",
                      "  pm.expect(Array.isArray(posts)).to.eql(true);",
                      "});"
                    ]
                  }
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "05 · Authentication",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "Basic auth folder",
          "auth": {
            "type": "basic",
            "basic": [
              { "key": "username", "value": "{{demoUser}}", "type": "string" },
              { "key": "password", "value": "{{demoPass}}", "type": "string" }
            ]
          },
          "item": [
            {
              "name": "Basic Auth (explicit)",
              "request": {
                "method": "GET",
                "auth": {
                  "type": "basic",
                  "basic": [
                    { "key": "username", "value": "{{demoUser}}", "type": "string" },
                    { "key": "password", "value": "{{demoPass}}", "type": "string" }
                  ]
                },
                "url": "{{jsonApi}}/users/1"
              },
              "event": [
                {
                  "listen": "test",
                  "script": {
                    "exec": [
                      "pm.test('User returned with Basic auth sent', function () {",
                      "  pm.expect(pm.response.json().username).to.eql(pm.response.json().username);",
                      "});"
                    ]
                  }
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "name": "Basic Auth (inherit)",
              "request": {
                "method": "GET",
                "url": "{{jsonApi}}/users/1",
                "description": "After import: set Auth to \"Inherit from parent\" to demo folder-level Basic auth."
              },
              "event": [
                {
                  "listen": "test",
                  "script": {
                    "exec": [
                      "pm.test('User returned via folder auth', function () {",
                      "  pm.expect(pm.response.json().username).to.eql(pm.response.json().username);",
                      "});"
                    ]
                  }
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "name": "Bearer token",
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "auth": {
              "type": "bearer",
              "bearer": [
                { "key": "token", "value": "{{demoToken}}", "type": "string" }
              ]
            },
            "url": "{{jsonApi}}/posts/1"
          },
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('Post returned with Bearer sent', function () {",
                  "  pm.expect(pm.response.json().id).to.eql(pm.response.json().id);",
                  "});"
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "name": "API key header",
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "auth": {
              "type": "apikey",
              "apikey": [
                { "key": "value", "value": "{{apiKey}}", "type": "string" },
                { "key": "key", "value": "X-Demo-Key", "type": "string" },
                { "key": "in", "value": "header", "type": "string" }
              ]
            },
            "url": "{{jsonApi}}/posts/1"
          },
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('Post returned with API key header sent', function () {",
                  "  pm.expect(pm.response.json().id).to.eql(pm.response.json().id);",
                  "});"
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "06 · Scripts & tests",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "Pre-request sets variable",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "prerequest",
              "script": {
                "exec": [
                  "pm.variables.set('greeting', 'Hello, Postchi!');"
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('Greeting echoed in response', function () {",
                  "  pm.expect(pm.response.json().title).to.eql('Hello, Postchi!');",
                  "});"
                ]
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              { "key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/json" }
            ],
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"title\": \"{{greeting}}\",\n  \"completed\": false,\n  \"userId\": 1\n}"
            },
            "url": "{{jsonApi}}/todos"
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "Chained: save then reuse id",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('Todo created', function () {",
                  "  var body = pm.response.json();",
                  "  pm.expect(body.id).to.eql(body.id);",
                  "  pm.variables.set('lastTodoId', String(body.id));",
                  "});"
                ]
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              { "key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/json" }
            ],
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"title\": \"Run collection runner\",\n  \"completed\": false,\n  \"userId\": 1\n}"
            },
            "url": "{{jsonApi}}/todos"
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "Chained: fetch saved todo",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "prerequest",
              "script": {
                "exec": [
                  "if (!pm.variables.get('lastTodoId')) {",
                  "  pm.variables.set('lastTodoId', '1');",
                  "}"
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('Todo id matches runtime var', function () {",
                  "  pm.expect(String(pm.response.json().id)).to.eql(pm.variables.get('lastTodoId'));",
                  "});"
                ]
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "url": "{{jsonApi}}/todos/{{lastTodoId}}"
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "GET photos (list)",
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "url": "{{jsonApi}}/photos?albumId=1"
          },
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('Photos for album 1', function () {",
                  "  var photos = pm.response.json();",
                  "  pm.expect(Array.isArray(photos)).to.eql(true);",
                  "  pm.expect(photos.length).to.be.above(0);",
                  "});"
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    }
  ]
}
